ssing\"\n      }\n    },\n    \"construction\": {\n      \"contract_value\": {\n        \"value\": null,\n        \"status\": \"missing\"\n      },\n      \"awarded_date\": {\n        \"value\": null,\n        \"status\": \"missing\"\n      },\n      \"started_date\": {\n        \"value\": null,\n        \"status\": \"missing\"\n      },\n      \"completion_date\": {\n        \"value\": null,\n        \"status\": \"missing\"\n      },\n      \"contractual_duration_days\": {\n        \"value\": null,\n        \"status\": \"missing\"\n      },\n      \"change_orders\": [],\n      \"actual_value\": {\n        \"value\": null,\n        \"status\": \"missing\"\n      }\n    }\n  },\n  \"taxonomy\": {\n    \"client_type\": [\"federal_navfac\"],\n    \"program_type\": [\"military_defense\"],\n    \"program_subtype\": [\"utilities_infrastructure\"],\n    \"disciplines\": [\n      \"structural_engineering\"\n    ],\n    \"sub_disciplines\": [\n      \"structural_foundation\",\n      \"structural_concrete\"\n    ],\n    \"building_systems\": [\n      \"foundations\",\n      \"foundations_deep\",\n      \"electrical_systems\",\n      \"electrical_lighting_exterior\"\n    ],\n    \"construction_scope\": [\n      \"concrete_scope\",\n      \"concrete_cast_in_place\",\n      \"electrical_lighting_scope\"\n    ],\n    \"delivery_method\": [\"design_build\"],\n    \"contract_vehicle\": [\"federal_task_order\"],\n    \"procurement_type\": [\"federal\"],\n    \"award_type\": [\"unknown_award_type\"],\n    \"project_status\": [\"design_complete\"],\n    \"bfa_role\": [\"subconsultant\"]\n  },\n  \"project_description\": {\n    \"value\": \"Bulk-fuel storage pipes at NAS Oceana run along a wooded area and have no lighting at the expansion joints. The expansion joints are checked for leaks at regular intervals each day. There are three locations that have expansion joints. The purpose of this project is to provide adequate solar lighting for checking for fuel leaks at the expansion joints after sunset. BFA provided structural engineering design for the three concrete pole foundations.\",\n    \"source\": \"SOW Part 3 §1.0 + BOD Scope of Work\",\n    \"quote\": \"Bulk-fuel storage pipes run along a wooded area and have no lighting at the expansion joints. The expansion joints are checked for leaks at regular intervals each day. A leak at an expansion joint will allow fuel to get in the waterway. There are three locations that have expansion joints. The purpose of this project is to provide adequate solar lighting for checking for fuel leaks at the expansion joints after sunset.\"\n  },\n  \"bfa_scope_detail\": {\n    \"value\": \"Structural design: construction documents for 3 light pole foundations, including calculations, drawings, and specifications. Foundations are concrete piers designed per UFC 3-301-01 and geotechnical recommendations by GEO Environmental Resources, Inc. Concrete strength F'c = 4,500 psi; pole foundations project 2'-0\" above grade; top 3'-0\" of soil resistance not considered per geotechnical engineer recommendations.\",\n    \"source\": \"BOD Scope of Work and Description of Work\",\n    \"quote\": \"Providing construction documents for the light pole foundations including calculations, drawings, specifications for 3 light pole foundations at fuel line expansion joints located at NASO, Virginia Beach, Virginia.\"\n  },\n  \"key_technical_requirements\": {\n    \"lighting_system\": \"Solar-powered LED area lighting system at each of the 3 expansion joint locations. Automatic controls, dusk-to-dawn operation with motion activation. Luminaire: die-cast aluminum housing, frosted acrylic/polycarbonate lens, solid-state LEDs at 4000K CCT, minimum 80 CRI, minimum 100 L/W efficacy, 12VDC electronic dimming driver, UL Listed for damp locations, DLC qualified.\",\n    \"solar_assembly\": \"150W crystalline solar cell assembly, minimum 164 A/h battery with lockable box (min 5-yr warranty), 25-yr panel warranty, UL 1703 / IEC 61215 / IEC 61730 CE certified.\",\n    \"poles\": \"Corrosion-resistant metal poles; no wooden poles; no direct bury; no square poles; maximum height approximately 13 feet; designed for 130 mph wind loading minimum.\",\n    \"source\": \"SOW Part 3 §D5020\"\n  },\n  \"design_criteria\": {\n    \"codes\": [\n      \"NAVFAC Planning & Design Policy\",\n      \"UFC 1-200-01 DOD Building Code with Change 3\",\n      \"FC 1-300-09N Navy and Marine Corps Design Procedures\",\n      \"UFC 3-301-01 Structural Engineering with Change 2\",\n      \"IBC/VCC 2021\",\n      \"ASCE/SEI 7-22\",\n      \"UFC 3-501-01 Electrical Engineering\"\n    ],\n    \"source\": \"BOD Design Criteria + SOW Part 3 §2.1 and §D50\",\n    \"quote\": \"UFC 1-200-01 DOD Building Code, with change 3\"\n  },\n  \"socioeconomic_participation\": [],\n  \"tenant_freeform_tags\": [\n    \"navfac\",\n    \"naso\",\n    \"nas_oceana\",\n    \"virginia_beach\",\n    \"solar_lighting\",\n    \"fuel_infrastructure\",\n    \"design_build\",\n    \"structural_subconsultant\",\n    \"pole_foundations\",\n    \"site_infrastructure\"\n  ],\n  \"key_personnel\": [],\n  \"key_personnel_pending\": [],\n  \"drawings\": {\n    \"sheets\": [],\n    \"facts_derived\": {\n      \"gross_square_footage\": {\n        \"value\": null,\n        \"status\": \"missing\",\n        \"notes\": \"Not applicable — site infrastructure project with no building\"\n      },\n      \"floor_count\": {\n        \"value\": null,\n        \"status\": \"missing\",\n        \"notes\": \"Not applicable\"\n      },\n      \"mep_system_inventory\": {\n        \"hvac\": [],\n        \"electrical\": [\n          \"Solar-powered LED exterior lighting at 3 expansion joint locations\",\n          \"150W crystalline solar panel assembly per location\",\n          \"Minimum 164 A/h battery assembly per location\",\n          \"Adaptive dusk-to-dawn / motion-activated lighting controls\"\n        ],\n        \"plumbing\": [],\n        \"fire_protection\": []\n      }\n    },\n    \"notes\": \"No drawing set was included in the intake documents. The BOD references BFA-prepared structural drawings for pole foundations but these were not present. The SOW attachments include schematic expansion joint location maps but no formal drawing set was provided.\"\n  },\n  \"conflict_flags\": [],\n  \"narratives\": {\n    \"full\": \"narratives/full.md\",\n    \"short\": \"narratives/short.md\",\n    \"bullets\": \"narratives/bullets.md\",\n    \"aspects\": {\n      \"schedule\": null,\n      \"technical\": null,\n      \"teaming\": null\n    }\n  }\n}"